  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping study horticulture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The fruit and vegetables sector in Moldova has significant potential to be a major force for the country&apos;s economic development, building on comparative advantages such as excellent soil quality and favourable climatic conditions. However, the sector&apos;s potential is obstructed by a number of factors including inadequate adoption of modern farming techniques and lack of access to essential inputs. This project aims to uncover the challenges and needs of the Moldovan fruit and vegetables sector, which could serve as entry points for the development of the sector. The project further seeks to identify opportunities for development of the fruit and vegetables sector which can be tapped into by partnerships between Moldovan and Dutch businesses, knowledge institutions and other organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
